                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6600baa7-7b1f-36d1-90c8-934c51b3af3b",
                        "entry_id": "9750e5fd-7db7-3f35-a6f6-ab9d773c8a0b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A miniature radio carried aloft (e.g. by an uncrewed balloon, an airdrop from a crewed aircraft, or a sounding rocket) to automatically transmit measurements of the upper air such as the wind speed, pressure, temperature, and relative humidity to a receiving station on the ground."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9cb4a286-1882-4318-a866-42865915fe6f",
                                "sense_id": "6600baa7-7b1f-36d1-90c8-934c51b3af3b",
                                "text": "1980, National Research Council (U.S.) Select Committee on the National Weather Service, Technological and Scientific Opportunities for Improved Weather and Hydrological Services in the Coming Decade, page 44,\nThe ultimate limitation of radiosonde networks is the impracticality of global deployment. […] Although, in principle, satellite soundings should be able to match radiosonde accuracies, in practice, they have errors of at least twice those of radiosondes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ba95dd71-b8ae-4a2c-82e0-d9c723471bd8",
                                "sense_id": "6600baa7-7b1f-36d1-90c8-934c51b3af3b",
                                "text": "Thus, the performance characteristics of radiosondes and the relative accuracy of radiosonde winds have been the subject of a great deal of scrutiny over the last few decades."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae8a505a-fb54-4db7-ac71-f26a9a6a51bb",
                                "sense_id": "6600baa7-7b1f-36d1-90c8-934c51b3af3b",
                                "text": "Sounding balloons carry a payload, usually a radiosonde, to heights of 30 km or more."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
